-# Cinemana TV v1.5.2 — merged playback and performance build
+# Cinemana TV v1.5.3 — merged playback and performance build
 
 This release combines the strongest parts of **v1.5.0** (faster home, remote-first player, exact seek and skip/undo UI) and **v1.4.10** (conservative treatment of post-credits story scenes and lower-overhead marker polling).
 
 ## Build and installation
 
 - On Windows with JDK 17+, Android SDK 35 and internet access for Gradle, run `RUN-FULL-TEST.cmd` to run regression tests and build a test-signed release APK. Use `BUILD-APK.cmd` to build without unit tests, or `BUILD-DEBUG-APK.cmd` for a debugging build.
-- Output from `RUN-FULL-TEST.cmd`: `output/CinemanaTV-v1.5.2-test.apk`.
-- `versionName = 1.5.1`, `versionCode = 46`; the app ID, storage, history, downloads and settings are unchanged.
+- Output from `RUN-FULL-TEST.cmd`: `output/CinemanaTV-v1.5.3-test.apk`.
+- `versionName = 1.5.3`, `versionCode = 48`; the app ID, storage, history, downloads and settings are unchanged.
 - The APK signing key may not match an older install. Back up app data before removing older versions.
 - Automatic mature scene skipping is only available with accurate saved or externally supplied ranges; no real-time video AI is used.
 
@@ -23,7 +23,7 @@
 - Settings controls and search remain remote accessible and retain the v1.4.6 two-pane design.
 - Mature content options: **Off**, **Skip marked scenes**, or **Hide mature titles**.
 - External player handoff is disabled in Skip Scenes mode because it cannot enforce local markers.
-- Skip marked scenes works only for *exact scene ranges*, entered **before viewing** using Player Settings → Scene markers → Start/End timestamps, or saved while watching. **There is no automatic explicit-scene detection or trusted online scene-timestamp database.** Unmarked scenes are not automatically skipped.
+- Skip mature scenes uses available community and previously saved scene ranges automatically; the manual timestamp editor has been removed. Public movie scene-marker sources are supported when matching timestamps are available. Unmarked scenes are not automatically skipped.
 - Hide titles uses provider age certificates and adult tags. It may miss incorrectly labeled titles; it is not a certified child-protection solution.
 - Existing downloads, watch history, player and saved data formats remain intact.
 
